# Never commit the Unity project's generated solution files
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Unity3D generated meta files for folders that are ignored
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta

# Crash reports
sysinfo.txt
crashlytics-build.properties

# Builds
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Asset licences — THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
#
# Raw third-party assets are not ours to redistribute. Mixamo's terms allow use
# in a shipped game but not redistribution of the raw FBX, and the same is true
# of most "free" Asset Store and marketplace content. Keep the originals out of
# the repo; the game ships them inside a build, which is a different thing.
#
# The Asset Store EULA is explicit — assets must be embedded in a larger product
# and must not comprise a substantial portion of it. Royalty-free to *ship* is
# not the same as free to redistribute. Viking Village and friends live here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Assets/ThirdParty/**
Assets/ThirdParty.meta
*.fbx
*.fbx.meta
*.mixamo

# Vendor audio — Sonniss GDC bundles, Freesound, anything we didn't record
# ourselves. The Sonniss licence covers shipping the game, not handing out the
# raw WAVs. ~208 GB of this lands at M0.
*.wav
*.wav.meta
*.aiff
*.aiff.meta
*.flac
*.flac.meta
*.mp3
*.mp3.meta
*.ogg
*.ogg.meta

# Exception: the tree pack — Assets/Art/Trees/ — which is CC BY 4.0. That licence
# permits redistribution outright, unlike everything above, whose terms cover
# shipping the game but not handing out the raw files. The attribution it requires
# lives in Assets/Art/SOURCES.md and has to reach the game's own credits before ship.
#
# This is the one place a whitelist is correct, because *.fbx is an *extension*
# rule: moving files into a different folder does not escape it, so the note below
# about keeping originals outside ignored folders cannot work for meshes. The path
# is deliberately narrow — one folder, one extension — so nothing else slips in.
# Note both lines: git needs the .meta whitelisted too, or the mesh arrives with no
# import settings and no obvious reason why.
!Assets/Art/Trees/**/*.fbx
!Assets/Art/Trees/**/*.fbx.meta

# Exception: audio we record or synthesise ourselves. When that exists, keep it
#            outside the ignored folders — e.g. Assets/Audio/Original/ — rather
#            than whitelisting individual extensions back in.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Design docs — these live in a separate private repository, not here.
# A guardrail, so a docs/ folder can't be committed to a public repo by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/docs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
